Perhaps instead of a polymorph intrinsic, make it like the ^T option if you 
have intrinsic teleport?  So the player can choose when to polymorph, but it
cost him spell points (whatever you want to call them.)  So a first level
player might be able to make one change, but it might be a long time before
he could do it again, so if he changed into something with too high a level
he might find himself stuck later on when the player reverted back to human
and could not change again.  (Or, the amount of energy required to
polymorph might be based on the difference in levels between the player and
the desired form.)  (You'd still have to watch out for players polymorphing
into (female) dragons and laying eggs for pets, thought there might be ways
around that. (Hmm... maybe have intrinsic aggravate monter when polymorphed,
as the player is not a 'normal' whatever?) (Hmph.  Something should be given
to male characters who can't do this sort of pet making.))

I believe the original poster was talking about magicians and stories... hmm..
prehaps make it so that you could only polymorph (with this built-in intrinsic)
into non-weapon/non-armor forms, not other intelligent beings.  A common tale
in those stories was that if you were killed as an ant, you were dead.  If this
class did not revert to human when HP goes to zero, but just dies, that might
help balance it out.  (i.e. a marilith is a useful form, but it only has around
what?  20-35 hp and can't wear a lot of armor (though oddly enough, it can
wear speed boots!)  Would having to decide to remain as you are with your
armor and 300hp, or less armor (though the marilith has a lower natural
AC), more attacks, but only 30hp?  Vampire lord is slightly better, but
still...)

